2026-11-13 20:22:29,759 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - These are routine materials for IT professionals working on government technology projects
2026-11-13 20:22:29,760 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 2. **Timestamp Discrepancies Are Normal Windows Behavior**:
2026-11-13 20:22:29,760 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - crtime/mtime differences are EXPECTED when copying files to removable media
2026-11-13 20:22:29,761 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Modification times are preserved; creation times reflect when files were written to new media
2026-11-13 20:22:29,761 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - 60-78 day gaps are consistent with file backup/archival operations, not evidence of manipulation
2026-11-13 20:22:29,762 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 3. **File Extension Mismatches Are Ambiguous**:
2026-11-13 20:22:29,762 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Could indicate deliberate obfuscation (suspicious)
2026-11-13 20:22:29,762 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Could result from automatic backup/archival tool behavior (common issue)
2026-11-13 20:22:29,763 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Could be from batch rename operations or format conversion errors
2026-11-13 20:22:29,763 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Similar patterns on both RM#2 and RM#3, suggesting coordinated backup rather than exfiltration
2026-11-13 20:22:29,764 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] 4. **Multi-Burn CD-R History Suggests Legitimate Archival**:
2026-11-13 20:22:29,764 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - 9 burn sessions over 3.5 months (2014-12-01 to 2015-03-24)
